"In light of this evening's events, I ask that all Americans commit with their whole hearts to resolving our differences.

You had Republicans, conservatives, liberals, progressives in that room, and there was a tremendous amount of love and coming together."

@POTUS @realDonaldTrump on the shooting at tonight's WHCD.

"Tonight was supposed to bring together the government and the press, and in one way, it did.

That's a room that was just totally unified, and it was a really beautiful thing to see."

@POTUS reflects on the events that just unfolded at the WHCD as he kicks off his address.

